t reproduces and under which display conditions.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 30 document high dpi coordin misalign repro owner charli document key doc 2030 last updat 2026 09 02 retrospect cover 2026 08 17 test log reproduct note for the high dpi coordin misalign report for ciph 46 first reproduc 2026 08 17 sourc id src gdoc 30 document high dpi coordin misalign repro owner charli document key doc 2030 last updat 2026 09 02 retrospect cover 2026 08 17 repro step 1 open a pdf on a display report a scale factor abov 10 test at 150 and 200 2 compar the redact preview overlay s report box coordin against the coordin the render librari report for the same region 3 at scale factor abov 10 the overlay box is offset from the actual text region with the offset grow a scale factor increas sourc id src gdoc 30 document high dpi coordin misalign repro owner charli document key doc 2030 last updat 2026 09 02 retrospect cover 2026 08 17 result the misalign reproduc consist at both test scale factor it doe not reproduc at 100 scale sourc id src gdoc 30 document high dpi coordin misalign repro owner charli document key doc 2030 last updat 2026 09 02 retrospect cover 2026 08 17 status root caus ha not been isol a part of this reproduct pas this note onli establish that the defect reproduc and under which display condit\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e99d1d8e8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-02-High-DPI-PDF-Rendering-Fixes-Review.md\", \"id\": \"a55699b32432c8bc\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.32594406994377, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.17461934277681435, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6790351, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-02-High-DPI-PDF-Rendering-Fixes-Review.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e99d1d8e8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-02-High-DPI-PDF-Rendering-Fixes-Review.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-02-High-DPI-PDF-Rendering-Fixes-Review.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 987, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:58\", \"token_count\": 453, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"Retrospective report on the third-party license audit under CIPH-40.\\n\\n## Limitation\\n\\nThis report does not certify overall license compliance. The parser-license question remains open.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"retrospect report on the third parti licens audit under ciph 40 limit this report doe not certifi overal licens complianc the parser licens question remain open\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9a8a8848a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-21-License-Compliance-Review-Review.md\", \"id\": \"d070d37a6418202b\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.32081943598789203, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.15056147998270294, \"vector_similarity\": 0.718088, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-21-License-Compliance-Review-Review.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9a8a8848a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-21-License-Compliance-Review-Review.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-21-License-Compliance-Review-Review.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1278, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:48\", \"token_count\": 583, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-31\\n\\n# Engineering Note: Async Job Scheduler\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2031\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-04 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-20)\\n\\nRetrospective note on the async job scheduler added 2026-08-20 to the batch API under CIPH-47, for higher throughput under concurrent load.\\n\\n## What was added\\n\\nAn asynchronous scheduler that accepts batch API jobs and dispatches them to worker threads without blocking the request path, building on the multi-threading work already integrated into the batch CLI.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-31\\n\\n# Engineering Note: Async Job Scheduler\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2031\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-04 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-20)\\n\\nRetrospective note on the async job scheduler added 2026-08-20 to the batch API under CIPH-47, for higher throughput under concurrent load.\\n\\n## Design\\n\\nJobs are queued with a job ID returned immediately to the caller; a separate status endpoint reports progress. Workers pull from the same queue used by the multi-threaded batch path.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-31\\n\\n# Engineering Note: Async Job Scheduler\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2031\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-04 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-20)\\n\\nRetrospective note on the async job scheduler added 2026-08-20 to the batch API under CIPH-47, for higher throughput under concurrent load.\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\nThis note covers the scheduler's implementation and design only. It does not cover any concurrency issues found during later evaluation of the scheduler under load; those are separate from what this note documents.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 31 engin note async job schedul owner bob document key doc 2031 last updat 2026 09 04 retrospect cover 2026 08 20 retrospect note on the async job schedul ad 2026 08 20 to the batch api under ciph 47 for higher throughput under concurr load what wa ad an asynchron schedul that accept batch api job and dispatch them to worker thread without block the request path build on the multi thread work alreadi integr into the batch cli sourc id src gdoc 31 engin note async job schedul owner bob document key doc 2031 last updat 2026 09 04 retrospect cover 2026 08 20 retrospect note on the async job schedul ad 2026 08 20 to the batch api under ciph 47 for higher throughput under concurr load design job are queu with a job id return immedi to the caller a separ status endpoint report progress worker pull from the same queue use by the multi thread batch path sourc id src gdoc 31 engin note async job schedul owner bob document key doc 2031 last updat 2026 09 04 retrospect cover 2026 08 20 retrospect note on the async job schedul ad 2026 08 20 to the batch api under ciph 47 for higher throughput under concurr load scope this note cover the schedul s implement and design onli it doe not cover ani concurr issu found dure later evalu of the schedul under load those are separ from what this note document\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9e90a788a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-04-Async-Batch-Processing-Review.md\", \"id\": \"0081bbcc02cb4f7b\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.319343797965831, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.16259041137975863, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6851017, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-04-Async-Batch-Processing-Review.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9e90a788a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-04-Async-Batch-Processing-Review.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-04-Async-Batch-Processing-Review.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 956, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:00:48\", \"token_count\": 412, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-18\\n\\n# Zero-Trust Node Sync: Handshake Prototype Notes\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2018\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-15 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-06)\\n\\nThis note looks back at the first authenticated handshake prototype built 2026-08-06 for CIPH-34 (Zero-Trust Node Sync), ahead of multi-site local deployments.\\n\\n## What was prototyped\\n\\nA handshake in which each node presents a signed challenge/response before either side accepts replication traffic from the other. No central node is required to bootstrap trust between two peers.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-18\\n\\n# Zero-Trust Node Sync: Handshake Prototype Notes\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2018\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-15 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-06)\\n\\nThis note looks back at the first authenticated handshake prototype built 2026-08-06 for CIPH-34 (Zero-Trust Node Sync), ahead of multi-site local deployments.\\n\\n## Result as of 2026-08-06\\n\\nThe handshake completed reliably across every run on a single LAN segment with nominal round-trip latency. No cross-node encryption mismatches or handshake rejections were seen at that stage.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-18\\n\\n# Zero-Trust Node Sync: Handshake Prototype Notes\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2018\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-15 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-06)\\n\\nThis note looks back at the first authenticated handshake prototype built 2026-08-06 for CIPH-34 (Zero-Trust Node Sync), ahead of multi-site local deployments.\\n\\n## Open question\\n\\nThe prototype has only been exercised on one LAN segment. Whether the handshake holds up across a simulated multi-site link with realistic latency and jitter has not been tested and is the planned next step before this can support multi-site rollout.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 18 zero trust node sync handshak prototyp note owner bob document key doc 2018 last updat 2026 08 15 retrospect cover 2026 08 06 this note look back at the first authent handshak prototyp built 2026 08 06 for ciph 34 zero trust node sync ahead of multi site local deploy what wa prototyp a handshak in which each node present a sign challeng respons befor either side accept replic traffic from the other no central node is requir to bootstrap trust between two peer sourc id src gdoc 18 zero trust node sync handshak prototyp note owner bob document key doc 2018 last updat 2026 08 15 retrospect cover 2026 08 06 this note look back at the first authent handshak prototyp built 2026 08 06 for ciph 34 zero trust node sync ahead of multi site local deploy result a of 2026 08 06 the handshak complet reliabl across everi run on a singl lan segment with nomin round trip latenc no cross node encrypt mismatch or handshak reject were seen at that stage sourc id src gdoc 18 zero trust node sync handshak prototyp note owner bob document key doc 2018 last updat 2026 08 15 retrospect cover 2026 08 06 this note look back at the first authent handshak prototyp built 2026 08 06 for ciph 34 zero trust node sync ahead of multi site local deploy open question the prototyp ha onli been exercis on one lan segment whether the handshak hold up across a simul multi site link with realist latenc and jitter ha not been test and is the plan next step befor this can support multi site rollout\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9dc21828a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-15-Zero-Trust-Node-Sync-Review.md\